# M-005 — Governed Automation Beta

**Status:** Planned  
**Target gate:** 2027-01-10 (forecast)  
**Increment:** PI-EXP-002  
**Product Goal:** PG-003

## Outcome

Monad can run consequential automation under signed attestations, cryptographic agility, strong identity, prompt/secret/capability security, declarative policy, formal change control, tamper-evident audit, readiness/done trust gates, OpenTelemetry, execution analytics, privacy-governed hosted analytics, and controlled shared deployment.

## Acceptance

- WC-EXP-0006 through WC-EXP-0009 accepted;
- WP-EXP-0013 through WP-EXP-0024 closed or explicitly replanned without weakening PG-003;
- attestation/identity/key lifecycle policies have conformance evidence;
- security boundaries withstand negative prompt/secret/capability tests;
- change/rollback/audit history is reconstructable;
- operational telemetry correlates actions to Work Packets/executions/evidence;
- hosted analytics/deployment remain optional and separable from local semantic authority.

